+Section 4 gives the positive algorithms. With a corresponding modulator,
+2-Subcoloring takes `2^O(k) n^O(1)` time (the theorem immediately before
+Theorem 7), yielding Theorem 7's `2^O(n^(1-1/(d+1)))` geometric algorithm.
+Theorem 8 gives `n^O(alpha-mod(G))` for Two Sets Cut-Uncut, and the following
+theorem specializes it to
