880:\subsection{Dichotomy for exactly six appearances per variable}\label{sub:six}
882:In this section, we settle the computational complexity status for \textsc{Monotone 3-Sat-E6}, i.e., with exactly $6$ variable appearances. From the previous section we know that \textsc{Monotone 3-Sat-($5,1$)}, and hence \textsc{Monotone 3-Sat-($1,5$)} are NP-complete (Theorem~\ref{thm:Mon3Sat-(1,5)}). From Section~\ref{sub:balanced} we can conclude that \textsc{Monotone 3-Sat-(3,3)} is NP-complete (Theorem~\ref{thm:Mon3Sat-(k,k)}). Clearly, if a variable appears only unnegated or only negated the problem becomes trivial. Therefore, it remains to establish the the computational complexity status for \textsc{Monotone 3-Sat-($4,2$)} (and hence for \textsc{Monotone 3-Sat-($2,4$)}). 
