Rejected at Step 0; no defensible G/H/V family survived.

Key findings from the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.26533):

- Theorem 1’s separator is produced by a polynomial-time histogram scan. At the output-cap boundary, both the mechanical and compact routes require the same 2,920 operations.
- Theorems 17 and 19 prove worst-case ETH hardness, not hardness for an inverse-planted distribution.
- The natural four-occurrence planted NAE-3-SAT distribution fell to DPLL on 8/8 instances; at 240 variables it required only 68–89 branch nodes.
- A literal coloring or cut from the paper’s reduction exceeds the 256-element answer cap while the source formula is still hand-trivial.
- Returning only the source assignment would compile away the geometric problem and become a convenience CSP surrogate.

The complete evidence and Track A/Track B analysis are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.26533/REJECTED.md). Per the instructions, no generator or oracle transcripts were created.
